# strih-lx -- the strih SNV Linux notebook (issue 1317; the production strih since the M4 cut-over
# 20.9.2026). Box FACTS for scripts/setup-strih.sh / scripts/verify-strih.sh (issue 1361).
#
# Format: plain KEY=value, one per line; `#` comment lines and blank lines are ignored. The value is
# everything after the first `=`, taken LITERALLY (no quotes, no `$`, no shell). The file is never
# executed -- scripts/lib/strih-box-facts.sh parses + validates it (unknown / missing / duplicate keys
# and a `TODO_OWNER` value all refuse). Run-time facts (PL1 watts, the CPU plan, the NIC interface
# name) are NOT here: setup-strih.sh derives them on the box.

# The box's own hostname = its fleet name = this file's name (DistroAV announces its outputs as
# "<HOSTNAME upper-cased> (...)"; the dev1 fleet list row is keyed on it).
STRIH_HOSTNAME=strih-lx
# The rig-LAN static IP (/23). Must equal the fleet list row when one exists (scripts/lib/obs-fleet.sh).
STRIH_IP=10.77.9.202
# NDI output name prefix: DistroAV prepends the hostname, so this MUST be STRIH_HOSTNAME upper-cased.
STRIH_NDI_PREFIX=STRIH-LX
# dantesync role: `server` = the fleet NTP master (bare daemon, no upstream); `client` = sync from
# STRIH_DANTESYNC_UPSTREAM (--ntp-server <host>). Empty upstream is only valid for `server`.
STRIH_DANTESYNC_ROLE=server
STRIH_DANTESYNC_UPSTREAM=
# The intercom hub routing file (repo-relative) installed as /etc/intercom-hub/intercom.toml.
STRIH_INTERCOM_CONFIG=intercom/intercom.strih-lx.toml
# NIC selection rule: the kernel DRIVER of the ONE rig NDI NIC; fallback = the interface carrying
# STRIH_IP. STRIH_NIC_IFACE=<iface> stays the run-time override. Since 29.9.2026 the rig NIC is a Ubiquiti
# UACC-Adapter-RJ45-USBC-5GE = Realtek RTL8157 USB 5 GbE (issue 1391; it replaced the RTL8156B 2.5 GbE).
STRIH_NIC_DRIVER=r8152
# The rig NIC's out-of-tree driver, built through DKMS from vendor/ by setup-strih step 1b: the in-tree
# driver of the 7.0 kernels has no RTL8157 id. `none` = the in-tree driver serves the rig NIC.
STRIH_NIC_OOT_DRIVER=realtek-r8152-2.21.4
# The lowest rig-NIC USB device speed verify-strih item 36 accepts, Mb/s (10000 = USB 3.2 Gen 2; `none`
# for a NIC that is not a USB device). The notebook's USB-C port trained the adapter at Gen 1 (5000) one
# way round, and at 5 GbE it then lost ~240 packets/s; flipped 180 degrees it trained at 10000 (29.9.2026).
STRIH_NIC_MIN_USB_MBPS=10000
# The lowest Ethernet link speed verify-strih item 36 accepts, Mb/s (5GBASE-T to the MikroTik S+RJ10).
STRIH_NIC_MIN_LINK_MBPS=5000
# OBS profile + scene-collection names strih-obs-start.sh launches with (when they exist on the box).
STRIH_OBS_PROFILE=strih-lx
STRIH_OBS_COLLECTION=strih-lx
# The cam box the NDI 6.3.2 runtime is copied from (setup-strih step 4b; STRIH_NDI_PEER overrides).
STRIH_NDI_RUNTIME_PEER=10.77.9.61
# The venue Bitfocus Companion CONTROLLER the Stream Deck satellite connects to.
STRIH_COMPANION_HOST=10.77.9.205
# The venue CG sender the `cg` / `CG-obs` inputs receive (`none` = no CG inputs at this venue).
# SongPlayer's program, never the cg OBS: owner decision 5.10.2026 (songplayer issue 221) moved every
# consumer off the cg OBS, which now feeds only SongPlayer's "OBS manual" input (issue 1403).
STRIH_CG_SENDER=RESOLUME-SNV (SP-program)
# The camera numbers N whose `CAMN (usb)` senders the strih receives as `NDI camN`.
STRIH_CAMERAS=1 2 3 4 5 6 7
# How the fixed HDMI output (~/.camera-box/drm-output.json) leaves the X desktop: `lease` = the X RandR
# lease (an Intel-driven connector, imag) or `vk-direct` = Vulkan direct display. The notebook's
# built-in HDMI is driven by the NVIDIA GPU, whose X driver refuses the lease (issue 1346).
STRIH_HDMI_OUTPUT_BACKEND=vk-direct
